-- title:
--   Proof of Theorem 5.10, p. 16 — (∫L)ₘ = (∫τ<ₙL)ₘ for n ≥ m
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a non-negatively graded $L_\infty$-algebra, finite dimensional in each degree, and fix $r \ge 1$. For all $m \le n$, the restriction map $\int L \to \int \tau_{<n}L$, induced by the inclusion $C^*(\tau_{<n}L) \subseteq C^*(L)$, is a bijection at level $m$:
--   $$\Big(\textstyle\int L\Big)_m = \Big(\textstyle\int \tau_{<n}L\Big)_m \qquad (n \ge m).$$
--
--   In the proof of Theorem 5.10 this transfers the Kan condition from the pieces $\int\tau_{<n}L$ to $\int L$: a horn at level $m$ only sees generators of degree $\le m$, on which $L$ and $\tau_{<n}L$ agree.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: an L∞-algebra: brackets [ ], [ , ], … of degrees −1, 0, 1, …, whose axioms are δ² = 0 for the induced derivation δ of C∗(L) (§1.1, p. 1); non-negatively graded, finite dimensional in each degree (p. 13) → L : ℕ → Type with FiniteDimensional ℝ (L i) for every i, and δ : LInfty L, a linear map of degree +1 on CE L that is a graded derivation with δ ∘ δ = 0; reason: §1.1: a degree-one derivation of C∗(L) with δ² = 0 is the same thing as the brackets with their axioms; no sign convention for the brackets is needed
--   - encoding: C∗(L) = Sym(L∨), graded-commutative, L∗ᵢ in degree i + 1 (§1.1, p. 1) → CE L = ExteriorAlgebra(⊕_{i even} L∗ᵢ) ⊗ SymmetricAlgebra(⊕_{i odd} L∗ᵢ), with the generator map gen and the degree pieces ceDeg; reason: generators of odd degree anticommute and those of even degree commute; the plain tensor product is the graded one because the symmetric factor is concentrated in even degrees
--   - encoding: the Postnikov pieces τ≤ₙL, τ<ₙL with the brackets inherited from L (Definition 5.6, p. 14), and ∫ of them → generator systems tauLe δ n, tauLt δ n: L∗ᵢ for i < n, kerSub δ n = ker ∂ₙ₊₁∗ resp. imSub δ n = im ∂ₙ∗ for i = n, 0 above (tauLt δ 0 = 0); ker ∂ₙ₊₁∗ = {ξ | δξ ∈ subalgebra generated by L∗_{≤n}}, im ∂ₙ∗ = {ξ | ∃ η ∈ L∗ₙ₋₁, δη − ξ ∈ subalgebra generated by L∗_{≤n−1}}; ∫ of a piece = DGA maps out of the subalgebra it generates; reason: the projection L → τL dualizes to an injective DGA map C∗(τL) → C∗(L) whose image is this subalgebra, since (coker ∂ₙ₊₁)∗ = ker ∂ₙ₊₁∗ and (im ∂ₙ)∗ ≅ (Lₙ/ker ∂ₙ)∗ = im ∂ₙ∗; the characterizations hold because the nonlinear part of δ on L∗ₙ only involves L∗_{≤n}, and they do not depend on the sign of the transpose
--   - encoding: de Rham forms on the m-simplex Δᵐ; Ωⁿ_{Cʳ}(M) = {α of class Cʳ | dα of class Cʳ} with its Banach topology (Convention 5.1, p. 13) → forms are ExteriorAlgebra((ℝᵐ)∗)-valued functions on ℝᵐ, only their values on the corner simplex {t ≥ 0, ∑ t ≤ 1} matter; d uses derivatives within Δᵐ; Ωⁿ_{Cʳ}(Δᵐ) = CrForms r m n, the closed span of the jets (all partial derivatives of order ≤ r of the coefficients of α and of dα, restricted to Δᵐ, sup norms); reason: this jet norm is equivalent to the Cʳ norm on α and dα; the jet image of these forms is closed, so the closed span is the space itself; faces are pullbacks along the affine cofaces of (3)
--   - encoding: (∫L)ₘ = Hom_DGA(C∗(L), Ω∗(Δᵐ)) (Definition 5.2, (20)) → integ r δ S m ⊆ Amb r S m: the tuples (φ(gen bₖ))_{i<m, k} of images of a chosen basis bₖ of each generator space S i, i < m, over the algebra maps φ from the subalgebra generated by S into forms that send L∗ᵢ to (i+1)-forms, take values in Ω∗_{Cʳ} and satisfy d ∘ φ = φ ∘ δ on Δᵐ (IsDGAMap); reason: a DGA map out of a free graded-commutative algebra is determined by the images of its generators, and generators of degree > m go to 0 on Δᵐ; the choice of basis changes no topology
--   - reading: the equality (∫L)ₘ = (∫τ<ₙL)ₘ for n ≥ m → the restriction map res : Amb r ⊤ m → Amb r (tauLt δ n) m is a bijection from integ r δ ⊤ m onto integ r δ (tauLt δ n) m (Set.BijOn); reason: the equality is the canonical map; res is a linear change of basis on the ambient spaces, so it identifies the two subsets as manifolds
-- source:
--   Henriques, Integrating L∞-algebras, arXiv:math/0603563v2, p. 16, proof of Theorem 5.10, first paragraph

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_IntLInfty_Kan_CE
import Definitions.Def_IntLInfty_Kan_Forms
import Definitions.Def_IntLInfty_Kan_Manifold
import Definitions.Def_IntLInfty_Kan_Integ

namespace IntLInfty.Kan

theorem proof_5_10_levels (r : ℕ) (hr : 1 ≤ r) (L : ℕ → Type) [∀ i, AddCommGroup (L i)]
    [∀ i, Module ℝ (L i)] [∀ i, FiniteDimensional ℝ (L i)] (δ : LInfty L) (m n : ℕ) (hmn : m ≤ n) :
    Set.BijOn (res (S := ⊤) (S' := tauLt δ n) (fun i => le_top) (r := r) (m := m))
      (integ r δ ⊤ m) (integ r δ (tauLt δ n) m) := by sorry

end IntLInfty.Kan
